#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/extracted-outputs/d0ad384b-c2f1-4bc6-8730-ec8a4b593a50-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/extracted-outputs/d0ad384b-c2f1-4bc6-8730-ec8a4b593a50-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default, states in Qiskit are initialized to the $|0\\rangle$ state. So it is no surprise that almost all of the first measurements yeilded $|0\\rangle$. Note however, that there was almost an even split in the second measurement (the one giving information about projections of the state onto $x$). It seems like this state that gives us a very predictable outcome of measurements along $z$ gives us a very unpredictable set of outcomes for measurements along $x$. Let's explore this.\n"
msgstr "Secara lalai, keadaan dalam Qiskit dimulakan kepada keadaan $|0\\rangle$. Jadi tidak hairanlah hampir semua pengukuran pertama menghasilkan $|0\\rangle$. Walau bagaimanapun, perhatikan bahawa terdapat hampir pembahagian sama rata dalam pengukuran kedua (yang memberi maklumat tentang unjuran keadaan pada $x$). Nampaknya keadaan yang memberi kita hasil pengukuran yang sangat dapat diramal sepanjang $z$ memberi kita set hasil yang sangat tidak dapat diramal untuk pengukuran sepanjang $x$. Mari kita terokai ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What happens if the make the measurements in the opposite order? We could start by using the Hadamard gate to obtain statistics on the probability of $|0\\rangle$ being measured in $|\\pm\\rangle_x$. Then for the second measurement, we will change back to the $z$ basis using a second Hadamard gate.\n"
msgstr "Apa yang berlaku jika kita membuat pengukuran dalam urutan yang bertentangan? Kita boleh mulakan dengan menggunakan get Hadamard untuk mendapatkan statistik mengenai kebarangkalian $|0\\rangle$ diukur dalam $|\\pm\\rangle_x$. Kemudian untuk pengukuran kedua, kita akan bertukar kembali ke asas $z$ menggunakan get Hadamard kedua.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/extracted-outputs/4029873f-1260-4fc3-bfd2-e5a3f579a09c-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/extracted-outputs/4029873f-1260-4fc3-bfd2-e5a3f579a09c-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/extracted-outputs/ce3fb0fd-a859-4c91-b2e5-c09343a397c2-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/extracted-outputs/ce3fb0fd-a859-4c91-b2e5-c09343a397c2-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we seem to have even less predictability! Previously, we at least knew what the outcome would be of the first measurement, now we have a fairly even distribution across all possible states. It's not too hard to see why this happened. We started in $|0\\rangle$, which is a 50-50 mixture of $|+\\rangle_x$ and $|-\\rangle_x$, according to\n"
"$$|0\\rangle=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|+\\rangle_x+|-\\rangle_x)$$\n"
"So clearly there should be equal probability of obtaining the + or - state (mapped to 0 and 1 in the chart) for the first measurement. The measurement along $x$ collapses the state into either an eigenstate $|+\\rangle_x$ or the eigenstate $|-\\rangle_x$. Each one of those states is a 50-50 mixture of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$, according to\n"
"$$|+\\rangle_x = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$$\n"
"$$|-\\rangle_x = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)$$\n"
"So once the system is in an eigenstate of $x$, clearly, measurements along $z$ will yield both $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$, and will do so with roughly equal probability.\n"
"So our first example showed us that some states will have very predictable outcomes of some measurements, but unpredictable outcomes for other measurements. The current example shows us that we can do worse than that. There are states that can give us unpredictable outcomes for both measurements, even if all we do is swap the order of the measurements. Let's investigate how certain or uncertain a quantity is for a given state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini, kita seolah-olah mempunyai kurang kebolehramalan! Sebelum ini, sekurang-kurangnya kita mengetahui apakah hasilnya untuk pengukuran pertama, kini kita mempunyai taburan yang agak sekata merentasi semua keadaan yang mungkin. Tidak terlalu sukar untuk melihat mengapa ini berlaku. Kita bermula dalam $|0\\rangle$, yang merupakan campuran 50-50 antara $|+\\rangle_x$ dan $|-\\rangle_x$, menurut\n"
"$$|0\\rangle=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|+\\rangle_x+|-\\rangle_x)$$\n"
"Jadi jelas terdapat kebarangkalian yang sama untuk memperoleh keadaan + atau - (dipetakan kepada 0 dan 1 dalam carta) untuk pengukuran pertama. Pengukuran sepanjang $x$ meruntuhkan keadaan ke dalam keadaan eigen $|+\\rangle_x$ atau keadaan eigen $|-\\rangle_x$. Setiap satu daripada keadaan tersebut merupakan campuran 50-50 antara $|0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle$, menurut\n"
"$$|+\\rangle_x = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$$\n"
"$$|-\\rangle_x = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)$$\n"
"Jadi apabila sistem berada dalam keadaan eigen $x$, jelas bahawa pengukuran sepanjang $z$ akan menghasilkan kedua-dua $|0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle$, dan akan berbuat demikian dengan kebarangkalian yang lebih kurang sama.\n"
"Jadi contoh pertama kita menunjukkan bahawa ada keadaan yang mempunyai hasil yang sangat dapat diramal untuk sesetengah pengukuran, tetapi hasil yang tidak dapat diramal untuk pengukuran lain. Contoh semasa menunjukkan kita boleh lebih teruk daripada itu. Terdapat keadaan yang boleh memberi kita hasil yang tidak dapat diramal untuk kedua-dua pengukuran, walaupun jika kita hanya menukar turutan pengukuran. Mari kita selidiki betapa pasti atau tidak pastinya suatu kuantiti bagi keadaan tertentu.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculating uncertainty {#calculating-uncertainty}"
msgstr "Mengira ketidakpastian {#calculating-uncertainty}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can quantify this using uncertainty, or variance. The \"uncertainty\" is often defined to be the square root of the \"variance\" of a distribution. That is, the uncertainty for some observable $S$ is denoted $\\Delta S$ and is given by\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh mengukur ini menggunakan ketidakpastian, atau varians. \"Ketidakpastian\" sering ditakrifkan sebagai punca kuasa dua \"varians\" suatu taburan. Iaitu, ketidakpastian untuk beberapa boleh cerap $S$ dinotasikan sebagai $\\Delta S$ dan diberikan oleh\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\Delta S)^2 & \\equiv \\langle (S - \\langle S \\rangle)^2 \\rangle\\\\\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\Delta S)^2 & \\equiv \\langle (S - \\langle S \\rangle)^2 \\rangle\\\\\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(\\Delta S)^2 & = \\langle S^2 - 2 S \\langle S \\rangle +\\langle S \\rangle^2 \\rangle\\\\\n"
msgstr "(\\Delta S)^2 & = \\langle S^2 - 2 S \\langle S \\rangle +\\langle S \\rangle^2 \\rangle\\\\\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(\\Delta S)^2 & = \\langle S^2 \\rangle - \\langle S \\rangle^2\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"(\\Delta S)^2 & = \\langle S^2 \\rangle - \\langle S \\rangle^2\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the case of Pauli matrices, for which $S^2 = I$, this becomes\n"
msgstr "Untuk kes matriks Pauli, yang mana $S^2 = I$, ini menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(\\Delta S)^2 = 1 - \\langle S \\rangle^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(\\Delta S)^2 = 1 - \\langle S \\rangle^2\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's apply this to a concrete example. Let's start with the state $|\\psi\\rangle = |+\\rangle_y = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ i \\end{pmatrix},$ and let's determine the uncertainty of the observable $X$ in that state.\n"
msgstr "Mari kita terapkan ini pada contoh konkrit. Mari kita mulakan dengan keadaan $|\\psi\\rangle = |+\\rangle_y = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ i \\end{pmatrix},$ dan mari kita tentukan ketidakpastian boleh cerap $X$ dalam keadaan tersebut.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding}"
msgstr "Uji kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the uncertainty of $X$ in the state $|+\\rangle_y = |+i\\rangle$, by hand.\n"
msgstr ""
"Baca soalan di bawah, fikirkan jawapan anda, kemudian klik segi tiga untuk mendedahkan penyelesaian.\n"
"Kira ketidakpastian $X$ dalam keadaan $|+\\rangle_y = |+i\\rangle$, secara tangan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Jawapan\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X =\\sqrt{\\langle+i| X^2 |+i\\rangle - \\langle+i| X |+i\\rangle^2}\n"
"$$\n"
"In the given state, this yields:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Delta X & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ i\\end{pmatrix} - \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ i\\end{pmatrix}\\right)^2}\\\\\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X =\\sqrt{\\langle+i| X^2 |+i\\rangle - \\langle+i| X |+i\\rangle^2}\n"
"$$\n"
"Dalam keadaan yang diberikan, ini menghasilkan:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Delta X & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ i\\end{pmatrix} - \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ i\\end{pmatrix}\\right)^2}\\\\\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\Delta X & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ i\\end{pmatrix} - \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}i \\\\ 1\\end{pmatrix}\\right)^2}\\\\\n"
msgstr "\\Delta X & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ i\\end{pmatrix} - \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}i \\\\ 1\\end{pmatrix}\\right)^2}\\\\\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\Delta X & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ i\\end{pmatrix} - \\left(\\frac{1}{2}(0))\\right)^2}\\\\\n"
msgstr "\\Delta X & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ i\\end{pmatrix} - \\left(\\frac{1}{2}(0))\\right)^2}\\\\\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\Delta X & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}(2)} = 1\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\Delta X & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}(2)} = 1\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can create an arbitrary initial state using ```qc.initialize()```. Note that the syntax for the imaginary unit here is $1j$.\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh mencipta keadaan awal yang sewenang-wenang menggunakan ```qc.initialize()```. Perhatikan bahawa sintaks untuk unit khayalan di sini ialah $1j$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"According to our equation above,\n"
"$$(\\Delta X)^2 = 1 - \\langle X \\rangle^2 = 1-(0.0015...)^2 \\rightarrow \\Delta X = 0.999...$$\n"
"Let's stick with that same state, but find the expectation value of $Z$, now:\n"
msgstr ""
"Menurut persamaan kita di atas,\n"
"$$(\\Delta X)^2 = 1 - \\langle X \\rangle^2 = 1-(0.0015...)^2 \\rightarrow \\Delta X = 0.999...$$\n"
"Mari kita kekal dengan keadaan yang sama, tetapi cari nilai jangkaan $Z$, sekarang:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We could do the same math as before, but we would see that the variance is again very close to 1.0. We could conclude that $\\Delta X \\Delta Z \\approx 1.0$. Indeed this approximately correct for the state we chose. But can we do better? Or worse?\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh melakukan matematik yang sama seperti sebelum ini, tetapi kita akan melihat bahawa varians kembali sangat hampir dengan 1.0. Kita boleh menyimpulkan bahawa $\\Delta X \\Delta Z \\approx 1.0$. Memang ini kira-kira betul untuk keadaan yang kita pilih. Tetapi bolehkah kita lakukan lebih baik? Atau lebih teruk?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that there is an uncertainty relation between position along one direction, $x,$ and momentum along the same direction, $p_x.$ For those variables, but most familiar form is probably\n"
"$$\\Delta x \\Delta p_x \\geq \\hbar/2$$\n"
"If this is all we remember, we might be tempted to think that $\\Delta X$ and $\\Delta Z$ could also have such a fundamental limit on uncertainty. Perhaps it is impossible for the product $\\Delta X \\Delta Z$ to reach zero? Let's try another state and see if this holds. This time, we'll use $|\\psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.$ Let's see what happens. Note that in the code below, estimator can accept two sets of circuits and observables in the same job submission.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ingat bahawa terdapat hubungan ketidakpastian antara kedudukan sepanjang satu arah, $x,$ dan momentum sepanjang arah yang sama, $p_x.$ Untuk pemboleh ubah tersebut, bentuk yang paling biasa adalah mungkin\n"
"$$\\Delta x \\Delta p_x \\geq \\hbar/2$$\n"
"Jika ini sahaja yang kita ingat, kita mungkin tergoda untuk berfikir bahawa $\\Delta X$ dan $\\Delta Z$ juga boleh mempunyai had asas sedemikian pada ketidakpastian. Mungkin adalah mustahil untuk hasil darab $\\Delta X \\Delta Z$ mencapai sifar? Mari kita cuba keadaan lain dan lihat sama ada ini berlaku. Kali ini, kita akan menggunakan $|\\psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.$ Mari lihat apa yang berlaku. Perhatikan bahawa dalam kod di bawah, estimator boleh menerima dua set litar dan boleh cerap dalam penghantaran kerja yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The expectation value of $X$ should be close to 1.0, but should not exceed 1.0. Don't worry if it exceeds 1.0 by a very small amount. This can be attributed to factors like noise and/or readout error. Although this is a very important topic, we can ignore it for now.\n"
msgstr "Nilai jangkaan $X$ sepatutnya hampir dengan 1.0, tetapi tidak seharusnya melebihi 1.0. Jangan risau jika ia melebihi 1.0 dengan jumlah yang sangat kecil. Ini boleh dikaitkan dengan faktor seperti hingar dan/atau ralat pembacaan. Walaupun ini adalah topik yang sangat penting, kita boleh mengabaikannya buat masa ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We obtained an expectation value of $X$ that is very close to 1.0 (corresponding to a very low variance for $X$). This makes the product of the two variances quite low:\n"
msgstr "Kita mendapat nilai jangkaan $X$ yang sangat hampir dengan 1.0 (sepadan dengan varians yang sangat rendah untuk $X$). Ini menjadikan hasil darab kedua-dua varians agak rendah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X \\Delta Z = \\sqrt{1-(0.9853)^2} \\times \\sqrt{1-(-0.00195)^2} = 0.171.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X \\Delta Z = \\sqrt{1-(0.9853)^2} \\times \\sqrt{1-(-0.00195)^2} = 0.171.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "While this is not exactly zero, this value is getting small in comparison with the eigenvalues of the Pauli operators ($\\pm 1$). Well, you may recall that the uncertainty relation between linear position and momentum could be written differently, explicitly using the commutation relation between the operators $x$ and $p_x$:\n"
msgstr "Walaupun ini bukan tepat sifar, nilai ini semakin kecil berbanding dengan nilai eigen operator Pauli ($\\pm 1$). Nah, anda mungkin ingat bahawa hubungan ketidakpastian antara kedudukan linear dan momentum boleh ditulis secara berbeza, secara eksplisit menggunakan hubungan penukaran antara operator $x$ dan $p_x$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta x \\Delta p_x \\geq \\frac{1}{2}|\\langle [x,p_x] \\rangle|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta x \\Delta p_x \\geq \\frac{1}{2}|\\langle [x,p_x] \\rangle|\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where\n"
msgstr "di mana\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"[x,p_x] = xp_x-p_xx\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"[x,p_x] = xp_x-p_xx\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "is the commutator of $x$ and $p_x$.\n"
msgstr "ialah penukaran bagi $x$ dan $p_x$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the form that that can be most easily extended to the Pauli operators. Generally, for two operators $A$ and $B$,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\Delta A \\Delta B \\geq \\frac{1}{2}|\\langle [A,B] \\rangle|.\n"
"$$\n"
"And in the case of the Pauli matrices $X$ and $Z$, we need $[X,Z]$ in order to calculate\n"
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X \\Delta Z \\geq \\frac{1}{2}|\\langle [X,Z] \\rangle|.\n"
"$$\n"
"We show this here, and leave similar calculations to the reader as an exercise:\n"
"$$\n"
"[X,Z] = XZ-ZX = \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}-\\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"[X,Z] = \\begin{pmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}-\\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} = 2\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"This is a perfectly acceptable answer, but with one more step, we see\n"
msgstr ""
"Inilah bentuk yang paling mudah dilanjutkan kepada operator Pauli. Secara umumnya, untuk dua operator $A$ dan $B$,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\Delta A \\Delta B \\geq \\frac{1}{2}|\\langle [A,B] \\rangle|.\n"
"$$\n"
"Dan dalam kes matriks Pauli $X$ dan $Z$, kita memerlukan $[X,Z]$ untuk mengira\n"
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X \\Delta Z \\geq \\frac{1}{2}|\\langle [X,Z] \\rangle|.\n"
"$$\n"
"Kita tunjukkan ini di sini, dan tinggalkan pengiraan yang serupa kepada pembaca sebagai latihan:\n"
"$$\n"
"[X,Z] = XZ-ZX = \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}-\\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"[X,Z] = \\begin{pmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}-\\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} = 2\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"Ini adalah jawapan yang boleh diterima sepenuhnya, tetapi dengan satu langkah lagi, kita melihat\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"[X,Z] = -2i\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}=-2iY\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"[X,Z] = -2i\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}=-2iY\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our uncertainty relation thus becomes\n"
msgstr "Hubungan ketidakpastian kita dengan itu menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X \\Delta Z \\geq |\\langle Y \\rangle|.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X \\Delta Z \\geq |\\langle Y \\rangle|.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-1}"
msgstr "Uji kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Determine $[X,Y]$ and $[Y,Z]$. Use this to write down the uncertainty relations between $X$ & $Y$, and $Y$ & $Z$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Baca soalan di bawah, fikirkan jawapan anda, kemudian klik segi tiga untuk mendedahkan penyelesaian.\n"
"Tentukan $[X,Y]$ dan $[Y,Z]$. Gunakan ini untuk menulis hubungan ketidakpastian antara $X$ & $Y$, dan $Y$ & $Z$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"[X,Y] = XY-YX = \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}-\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} = 2 \\begin{pmatrix}i & 0 \\\\ 0 & -i\\end{pmatrix}=2iZ\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"[X,Y] = XY-YX = \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}-\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} = 2 \\begin{pmatrix}i & 0 \\\\ 0 & -i\\end{pmatrix}=2iZ\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"[Y,Z] = YZ-ZY = \\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}-\\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix} = 2 \\begin{pmatrix}0 & i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}=2iX\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"[Y,Z] = YZ-ZY = \\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}-\\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix} = 2 \\begin{pmatrix}0 & i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}=2iX\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Combining with the general uncertainty relation, we have\n"
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X \\Delta Y \\geq |\\langle Z \\rangle|,\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"\\Delta Y \\Delta Z \\geq |\\langle X \\rangle|.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggabungkan dengan hubungan ketidakpastian umum, kita mendapat\n"
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X \\Delta Y \\geq |\\langle Z \\rangle|,\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"\\Delta Y \\Delta Z \\geq |\\langle X \\rangle|.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verify consistency {#verify-consistency}"
msgstr "Sahkan konsistensi {#verify-consistency}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before moving on, let us check that this was consistent with our previous finding. We used the state $|\\psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.$ And we found that $\\Delta X \\Delta Z  = 0.171.$ Now we know this product should be greater than or equal to\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\langle Y \\rangle|=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\langle Y \\rangle| = \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix} -i \\\\ i \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{1}{2}(-i+i) = 0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebelum meneruskan, mari kita semak bahawa ini konsisten dengan penemuan kita sebelumnya. Kita menggunakan keadaan $|\\psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.$ Dan kita mendapati bahawa $\\Delta X \\Delta Z  = 0.171.$ Kini kita tahu hasil darab ini seharusnya lebih besar atau sama dengan\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\langle Y \\rangle|=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\langle Y \\rangle| = \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix} -i \\\\ i \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{1}{2}(-i+i) = 0.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So indeed, $\\Delta X \\Delta Z  = 0.171 \\geq |\\langle Y \\rangle|=0$\n"
"Use the questions below to build some intuition for these findings:\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi memang, $\\Delta X \\Delta Z  = 0.171 \\geq |\\langle Y \\rangle|=0$\n"
"Gunakan soalan di bawah untuk membina intuisi tentang penemuan-penemuan ini:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-2}"
msgstr "Uji kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-2}"

# doq-bootstrap: msgid repeated on page, first translation kept
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Answer the following items together as a set:\n"
msgstr ""
"Baca soalan-soalan di bawah, fikirkan jawapan anda, kemudian klik segi tiga untuk mendedahkan penyelesaian.\n"
"Jawab item-item berikut bersama-sama sebagai satu set:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(a) What states would you expect to have zero uncertainty in $X$?\n"
msgstr "(a) Keadaan apakah yang anda jangkakan mempunyai ketidakpastian sifar dalam $X$?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(b) What states would you expect to have zero uncertainty in $Z$?\n"
msgstr "(b) Keadaan apakah yang anda jangkakan mempunyai ketidakpastian sifar dalam $Z$?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(c) In what states would you obtain a zero expectation value $\\langle Y \\rangle$?\n"
msgstr "(c) Dalam keadaan apakah anda akan mendapat nilai jangkaan sifar $\\langle Y \\rangle$?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(d) Are the answers to the above questions consistent with the case $\\Delta X \\Delta Z \\geq |\\langle Y \\rangle|$?\n"
msgstr "(d) Adakah jawapan kepada soalan-soalan di atas konsisten dengan kes $\\Delta X \\Delta Z \\geq |\\langle Y \\rangle|$?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(e) Write code to explicitly check this using estimator.\n"
msgstr "(e) Tulis kod untuk menyemak ini secara eksplisit menggunakan estimator.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(a) We might expect eigenstates of the $X$ operator to yield zero uncertainty in $X$. Indeed, using $|\\psi\\rangle = |+\\rangle_x,$ we have\n"
"$$\\Delta X = \\sqrt{1-\\langle X \\rangle^2} = \\sqrt{1-1^2} = 0.$$\n"
msgstr ""
"(a) Kita mungkin mengharapkan keadaan eigen operator $X$ menghasilkan ketidakpastian sifar dalam $X$. Memang, menggunakan $|\\psi\\rangle = |+\\rangle_x,$ kita mendapat\n"
"$$\\Delta X = \\sqrt{1-\\langle X \\rangle^2} = \\sqrt{1-1^2} = 0.$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(b) We might expect eigenstates of the $Z$ operator to yield zero uncertainty in $Z$. Indeed, using $|\\psi\\rangle = |1\\rangle,$ we have\n"
"$$\\Delta Z = \\sqrt{1-\\langle Z \\rangle^2} = \\sqrt{1-(-1)^2} = 0.$$\n"
msgstr ""
"(b) Kita mungkin mengharapkan keadaan eigen operator $Z$ menghasilkan ketidakpastian sifar dalam $Z$. Memang, menggunakan $|\\psi\\rangle = |1\\rangle,$ kita mendapat\n"
"$$\\Delta Z = \\sqrt{1-\\langle Z \\rangle^2} = \\sqrt{1-(-1)^2} = 0.$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(c) We expect to find $\\langle Y \\rangle=0$ for any states that, when measured, yield a positive projection on the $y$ axis just as often as a negative projection. These include the eigenstates of $X$ and $Z$.\n"
msgstr "(c) Kita jangkakan mendapat $\\langle Y \\rangle=0$ untuk sebarang keadaan yang, apabila diukur, menghasilkan unjuran positif pada paksi $y$ sama kerap dengan unjuran negatif. Ini termasuk keadaan eigen bagi $X$ dan $Z$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(d) Yes. One would expect a very small value for the product of uncertainties $\\Delta X \\Delta Z $ for eigenstates of $X$ or $Z$: $\\Delta X \\Delta Z \\approx 0.$ This can hold because we would also expect $\\langle Y \\rangle=0$ for those same states. So the uncertainty relation could be satisfied.\n"
msgstr "(d) Ya. Seseorang jangka nilai yang sangat kecil untuk hasil darab ketidakpastian $\\Delta X \\Delta Z $ bagi keadaan eigen $X$ atau $Z$: $\\Delta X \\Delta Z \\approx 0.$ Ini boleh berlaku kerana kita juga jangkakan $\\langle Y \\rangle=0$ untuk keadaan-keadaan yang sama. Jadi hubungan ketidakpastian boleh dipenuhi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(e) Code such as the following would verify this:\n"
msgstr "(e) Kod seperti berikut akan mengesahkan ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where the results returns all expectation values. To retrieve all expectation values and calculate uncertainties, we could use:\n"
msgstr "Di mana hasilnya mengembalikan semua nilai jangkaan. Untuk mendapatkan semua nilai jangkaan dan mengira ketidakpastian, kita boleh menggunakan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(a) Can you think of a state in which you would have a large expectation value $\\langle Y \\rangle$?\n"
msgstr "(a) Bolehkah anda fikirkan satu keadaan di mana anda akan mempunyai nilai jangkaan yang besar $\\langle Y \\rangle$?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(b) Would you expect that same state to have large or small uncertainty in $X$?\n"
msgstr "(b) Adakah anda jangkakan keadaan yang sama mempunyai ketidakpastian besar atau kecil dalam $X$?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(c) Would you expect that same state to have large or small uncertainty in $Z$?\n"
msgstr "(c) Adakah anda jangkakan keadaan yang sama mempunyai ketidakpastian besar atau kecil dalam $Z$?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(a) We expect to find $\\langle Y \\rangle\\approx 1$ for the eigenstate of $Y$: $|+\\rangle_y$.\n"
msgstr "(a) Kita jangkakan mendapat $\\langle Y \\rangle\\approx 1$ untuk keadaan eigen $Y$: $|+\\rangle_y$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(b) We might expect $X$ to have large uncertainty in the state $|+\\rangle_y,$ since measuring $X$ in that state would yield a positive and negative result with equal frequency/probability.\n"
msgstr "(b) Kita mungkin jangkakan $X$ mempunyai ketidakpastian besar dalam keadaan $|+\\rangle_y,$ kerana mengukur $X$ dalam keadaan itu akan menghasilkan keputusan positif dan negatif dengan frekuensi/kebarangkalian yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(c) We might expect $Z$ to have large uncertainty in the state $|+\\rangle_y,$ since measuring $Z$ in that state would yield a positive and negative result with equal frequency/probability.\n"
msgstr "(c) Kita mungkin jangkakan $Z$ mempunyai ketidakpastian besar dalam keadaan $|+\\rangle_y,$ kerana mengukur $Z$ dalam keadaan itu akan menghasilkan keputusan positif dan negatif dengan frekuensi/kebarangkalian yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(d) Yes. One would expect a large value for the product of uncertainties $\\Delta X \\Delta Z $ for eigenstates of $Y,$ and for $|+\\rangle_y,$ specifically. We would also expect $\\langle Y \\rangle\\approx 1$ for that same state. So both $\\langle Y \\rangle$ and $\\Delta X \\Delta Z $ are both fairly large in this state, and it is plausible that the uncertainty relation could again be satisfied.\n"
msgstr "(d) Ya. Seseorang jangka nilai yang besar untuk hasil darab ketidakpastian $\\Delta X \\Delta Z $ bagi keadaan eigen $Y,$ dan untuk $|+\\rangle_y,$ khususnya. Kita juga jangkakan $\\langle Y \\rangle\\approx 1$ untuk keadaan yang sama. Jadi kedua-dua $\\langle Y \\rangle$ dan $\\Delta X \\Delta Z $ adalah agak besar dalam keadaan ini, dan adalah munasabah bahawa hubungan ketidakpastian boleh dipenuhi sekali lagi.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Testing uncertainty relations {#testing-uncertainty-relations}"
msgstr "Menguji hubungan ketidakpastian {#testing-uncertainty-relations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The test above only demonstrated the validity of the uncertainty relation for a single choice of state vector $|\\psi\\rangle = |+\\rangle_x$. To convince ourselves that this is generally consistent with experiment, we should carry out similar calculations using estimator for many choices of the state vector. Let's start by rotating our state vector away from the $z$ axis, using an ```RY``` gate to produce different initial states using a parameter $\\theta$.\n"
msgstr "Ujian di atas hanya menunjukkan kesahihan hubungan ketidakpastian untuk satu pilihan vektor keadaan $|\\psi\\rangle = |+\\rangle_x$. Supaya kita lebih yakin bahawa ini secara amnya konsisten dengan eksperimen, kita perlu menjalankan pengiraan serupa menggunakan Estimator untuk pelbagai pilihan vektor keadaan. Mari kita mulakan dengan memutar vektor keadaan kita menjauhi paksi $z$, menggunakan get ```RY``` untuk menghasilkan keadaan awal yang berbeza menggunakan parameter $\\theta$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/extracted-outputs/1599d4df-38f8-4171-95ae-6c3c61409201-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/extracted-outputs/1599d4df-38f8-4171-95ae-6c3c61409201-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that the red curve $(\\Delta X \\Delta Z)$ is always greater than the orange curve $\\langle Y \\rangle.$ Sometimes the uncertainty product dips and is somewhat close to the limit, and other times it rises and is farther from the limit, but it always obeys the uncertainty relation.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bahawa lengkung merah $(\\Delta X \\Delta Z)$ sentiasa lebih besar daripada lengkung oren $\\langle Y \\rangle.$ Kadang-kadang hasil darab ketidakpastian menurun dan agak hampir dengan had, dan kadang-kadang ia naik dan lebih jauh dari had, tetapi ia sentiasa mematuhi hubungan ketidakpastian.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Of course, this might not be the best test of the uncertainty relation, since our limit $\\langle Y \\rangle$ is always very close to zero. Let's use a quantum state that has a larger projection on eigenstates of $Y$. Specifically, we will still rotate rotate $|0\\rangle$ down from the $z$ axis by varying angles, but now we will also rotate that resulting state around $z$ by some angle, perhaps $\\pi/4$, and see what happens.\n"
msgstr "Sudah tentu, ini mungkin bukan ujian terbaik bagi hubungan ketidakpastian, memandangkan had kita $\\langle Y \\rangle$ sentiasa sangat hampir dengan sifar. Mari kita gunakan keadaan kuantum yang mempunyai unjuran lebih besar pada keadaan eigen $Y$. Khususnya, kita masih akan memutar $|0\\rangle$ menjauhi paksi $z$ pada sudut yang berbeza-beza, tetapi kini kita juga akan memutar keadaan tersebut mengelilingi $z$ pada sudut tertentu, mungkin $\\pi/4$, dan lihat apa yang berlaku.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/extracted-outputs/6f129a2d-e029-45b7-bb77-bfa83babd8c9-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/extracted-outputs/6f129a2d-e029-45b7-bb77-bfa83babd8c9-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we see that the limit on the uncertainty $(\\Delta X \\Delta Z)$ is being put to the test! The red curve comes much closer to the orange curve than before. In fact, in the absence of noise, the uncertainty relation would be exactly saturated ($(\\Delta X \\Delta Z) = \\langle Y \\rangle$) one point. In the presence of noise and readout error, it should not be surprising if a run occasionally yields $(\\Delta X \\Delta Z)$ very slightly larger than $\\langle Y \\rangle.$ This is not a true violation of uncertainty; it is just an artifact of non-zero error.\n"
msgstr "Kini kita dapat lihat bahawa had ketidakpastian $(\\Delta X \\Delta Z)$ sedang diuji dengan lebih ketat! Lengkung merah kini jauh lebih hampir dengan lengkung oren berbanding sebelum ini. Bahkan, tanpa kehadiran hingar, hubungan ketidakpastian akan tepat-tepat tepu ($(\\Delta X \\Delta Z) = \\langle Y \\rangle$) pada satu titik. Dengan kehadiran hingar dan ralat pembacaan, tidak menghairankan jika sesuatu larian sesekali menghasilkan $(\\Delta X \\Delta Z)$ yang sedikit lebih besar daripada $\\langle Y \\rangle.$ Ini bukan pelanggaran sebenar terhadap ketidakpastian; ia hanyalah kesan sampingan daripada ralat yang tidak sifar.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-3}"
msgstr "Semak kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-3}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Explain how you would push this to the absolute limit, making $\\langle Y \\rangle$ as large as possible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Baca soalan-soalan di bawah, fikirkan jawapan anda, kemudian klik segi tiga untuk mendedahkan penyelesaiannya.\n"
"Terangkan bagaimana anda akan mendorong ini ke had mutlak, menjadikan $\\langle Y \\rangle$ sebesar mungkin?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The code currently has lines that rotate the default initial state $|0\\rangle$, down from the $z$ axis by some parametrized angle $\\theta$ and then also around the $z$ axis by an angle $\\pi/4,$ which rotates the state vector part of the way over to the $y$ axis.\n"
msgstr "Kod ini kini mempunyai baris-baris yang memutar keadaan awal lalai $|0\\rangle$, turun dari paksi $z$ pada sudut berparameter $\\theta$ dan kemudian juga mengelilingi paksi $z$ pada sudut $\\pi/4,$ yang memutar vektor keadaan sebahagian jalan ke arah paksi $y$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`qc.ry(theta,0)`\n"
msgstr "`qc.ry(theta,0)`\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`qc.rz(pi/4,0)`\n"
msgstr "`qc.rz(pi/4,0)`\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We could change the rotation about $z$ from $\\pi/4$ to $\\pi/2$, rotating all the way to an eigenstate of $Y$:\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh menukar putaran sekitar $z$ dari $\\pi/4$ kepada $\\pi/2$, memutar sepenuhnya ke keadaan eigen $Y$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`qc.rz(pi/2,0)`\n"
msgstr "`qc.rz(pi/2,0)`\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "No other changes would be required.\n"
msgstr "Tiada perubahan lain yang diperlukan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Change the code or copy it over and implement that check of the uncertainty relation with the expectation value of Y maximized. Does the uncertainty relation hold?\n"
msgstr "Ubah kod atau salin kod tersebut dan laksanakan pemeriksaan hubungan ketidakpastian dengan nilai jangkaan Y yang dimaksimumkan. Adakah hubungan ketidakpastian masih berlaku?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We would use exactly the code from the example above, with\n"
msgstr "Kita akan menggunakan kod dari contoh di atas, dengan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "swapped in to replace\n"
msgstr "digantikan untuk menggantikan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`qc.rz(pi/4,0).`\n"
msgstr "`qc.rz(pi/4,0).`\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid " The resulting figure should look like that below, and yes, the uncertainty principle should still be valid.\n"
msgstr " Rajah yang terhasil seharusnya kelihatan seperti yang di bawah, dan ya, prinsip ketidakpastian masih harus sah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid " ![A plot comparing uncertainty to the maximum expectation value of the Y operator.](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/checkin.avif)\n"
msgstr " ![A plot comparing uncertainty to the maximum expectation value of the Y operator.](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/checkin.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Modify the code above to make a similar picture, demonstrating that from measurements on the quantum computer the product $\\Delta X \\Delta Y$ behaves as it should. Choose any set of states you like.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Ubah suai kod di atas untuk membuat gambar yang serupa, menunjukkan bahawa dari pengukuran pada komputer kuantum, hasil darab $\\Delta X \\Delta Y$ berkelakuan sebagaimana mestinya. Pilih mana-mana set keadaan yang anda suka.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We would use exactly the code from the example above, and in face we could use the same results from above, just using the expectation values to calculate different uncertainties. For example, we could use\n"
msgstr "Kita akan menggunakan kod dari contoh di atas, dan sebenarnya kita boleh menggunakan keputusan yang sama dari atas, hanya menggunakan nilai jangkaan untuk mengira ketidakpastian yang berbeza. Sebagai contoh, kita boleh menggunakan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and we could plot\n"
msgstr "dan kita boleh plot\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Challenge: Write code to scan through many values of $\\phi$, just as we scanned through many values of $\\theta$, and make a 3-D plot showing that the uncertainty relation is never violated. Pick any observables you like.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Cabaran: Tulis kod untuk mengimbas pelbagai nilai $\\phi$, sama seperti kita mengimbas pelbagai nilai $\\theta$, dan buat plot 3-D yang menunjukkan bahawa hubungan ketidakpastian tidak pernah dilanggar. Pilih mana-mana boleh cerap yang anda suka.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Questions {#questions}"
msgstr "Soalan {#questions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instructors can request versions of these notebooks with answer keys and guidance on placement in common curricula by filling out this [quick survey](https://ibm.biz/classrooms_instructor_key_request) on how the notebooks are being used.\n"
msgstr "Pengajar boleh meminta versi buku nota ini dengan kunci jawapan dan panduan penempatan dalam kurikulum biasa dengan mengisi [tinjauan ringkas](https://ibm.biz/classrooms_instructor_key_request) ini tentang cara buku nota digunakan.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Critical concepts: {#critical-concepts}"
msgstr "Konsep utama: {#critical-concepts}"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are uncertainty relations between many sets of physical observables, including position & linear momentum, and components of spin.\n"
msgstr "Terdapat hubungan ketidakpastian antara banyak set boleh cerap fizikal, termasuk kedudukan & momentum linear, dan komponen spin.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Pauli matrices do not commute. This is a mathematical reflection of the fact that not all components of spin can be simultaneously known/determined.\n"
msgstr "Matriks Pauli tidak bertukar tertib. Ini adalah cerminan matematik daripada hakikat bahawa tidak semua komponen spin boleh diketahui/ditentukan secara serentak.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum computing makes heavy use of the Pauli operators/matrices, so it is useful to know the uncertainty relation for Pauli operators, as well as the closely-related spin operators.\n"
msgstr "Pengkomputeran kuantum banyak menggunakan operator/matriks Pauli, jadi adalah berguna untuk mengetahui hubungan ketidakpastian bagi operator Pauli, serta operator spin yang berkait rapat dengannya.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A general formula for the uncertainty of two operators $A$ and $B$ is $$\\Delta A \\Delta B \\geq \\frac{1}{2}|\\langle [A,B] \\rangle|.$$\n"
msgstr "Formula umum untuk ketidakpastian dua operator $A$ dan $B$ ialah $$\\Delta A \\Delta B \\geq \\frac{1}{2}|\\langle [A,B] \\rangle|.$$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An eigenstate $|a\\rangle$ of some operator $A$ yields zero uncertainty in the physical observable associated with that operator. Even experimentally, $\\Delta A \\approx 0.$\n"
msgstr "Keadaan eigen $|a\\rangle$ bagi sesuatu operator $A$ menghasilkan ketidakpastian sifar dalam boleh cerap fizikal yang berkaitan dengan operator tersebut. Walaupun secara eksperimen, $\\Delta A \\approx 0.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An eigenstate $|a\\rangle$ of some operator $A$ will yield a larger uncertainty for an operator $B$ that does not commute with $A$.\n"
msgstr "Keadaan eigen $|a\\rangle$ bagi sesuatu operator $A$ akan menghasilkan ketidakpastian yang lebih besar bagi operator $B$ yang tidak bertukar tertib dengan $A$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Experimental results using a real quantum computer confirm the intuition we gain from matrix representations of physical operators.\n"
msgstr "Keputusan eksperimen menggunakan komputer kuantum sebenar mengesahkan intuisi yang kita perolehi daripada perwakilan matriks operator fizikal.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F Questions: {#tf-questions}"
msgstr "Soalan B/S: {#tf-questions}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F One can simultaneously measure $X$ and $Y$, but not $Z$.\n"
msgstr "B/S Seseorang boleh mengukur $X$ dan $Y$ secara serentak, tetapi bukan $Z$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F One can simultaneously measure $X$ and $Z$, but not $Y$.\n"
msgstr "B/S Seseorang boleh mengukur $X$ dan $Z$ secara serentak, tetapi bukan $Y$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F Linear position and linear momentum operators do not commute.\n"
msgstr "B/S Operator kedudukan linear dan momentum linear tidak bertukar tertib.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F IBM quantum computers measure along $Z$ by default, so a rotation must be performed to measure along any other direction.\n"
msgstr "B/S Komputer kuantum IBM mengukur sepanjang $Z$ secara lalai, jadi putaran mesti dilakukan untuk mengukur sepanjang arah lain.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F The circuit below effectively measures $Z$ and then $X$.\n"
msgstr "B/S Litar di bawah secara berkesan mengukur $Z$ kemudian $X$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A circuit diagram showing a measurement, a Hadamard gate, and then another measurement.](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/tf-q5.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Gambar rajah litar yang menunjukkan pengukuran, get Hadamard, kemudian pengukuran lain.](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/tf-q5.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "MC Questions: {#mc-questions}"
msgstr "Soalan Aneka Pilihan: {#mc-questions}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The diagram below demonstrates which of the following uncertainty relations?\n"
msgstr "Rajah di bawah menunjukkan hubungan ketidakpastian yang mana antara berikut?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "a. $\\Delta X \\Delta Y \\geq |\\langle Z \\rangle|$\n"
msgstr "a. $\\Delta X \\Delta Y \\geq |\\langle Z \\rangle|$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "b. $\\Delta Y \\Delta Z \\geq |\\langle X \\rangle|$\n"
msgstr "b. $\\Delta Y \\Delta Z \\geq |\\langle X \\rangle|$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "c. $\\Delta Z \\Delta X \\geq |\\langle Y \\rangle|$\n"
msgstr "c. $\\Delta Z \\Delta X \\geq |\\langle Y \\rangle|$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "d. None of the above\n"
msgstr "d. Tiada yang di atas\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A plot comparing uncertainty to the maximum expectation value of the Y operator.](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/checkin.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Plot yang membandingkan ketidakpastian dengan nilai jangkaan maksimum bagi operator Y.](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/checkin.avif)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Which of the following is the standard sequence to perform a measurement along $x$?\n"
msgstr "Yang manakah antara berikut merupakan urutan standard untuk melakukan pengukuran sepanjang $x$?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "a. Only ```qc.measure()```\n"
msgstr "a. Hanya ```qc.measure()```\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "b. ```qc.h()``` then ```qc.measure()```\n"
msgstr "b. ```qc.h()``` kemudian ```qc.measure()```\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "c. ```qc.h()```, ```qc.h()``` then ```qc.measure()```\n"
msgstr "c. ```qc.h()```, ```qc.h()``` kemudian ```qc.measure()```\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "d. ```qc.h()```, ```qc.s```, ```qc.h()```then ```qc.measure()```\n"
msgstr "d. ```qc.h()```, ```qc.s```, ```qc.h()``` kemudian ```qc.measure()```\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "e. ```qc.sdg()```, ```qc.h()```, ```qc.s``` then ```qc.measure()```\n"
msgstr "e. ```qc.sdg()```, ```qc.h()```, ```qc.s``` kemudian ```qc.measure()```\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "f. ```qc.sdg()```, ```qc.h()```, ```qc.s```, ```qc.h()``` then ```qc.measure()```\n"
msgstr "f. ```qc.sdg()```, ```qc.h()```, ```qc.s```, ```qc.h()``` kemudian ```qc.measure()```\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Which of the following states yields the largest expectation value $\\langle X \\rangle$?\n"
msgstr "Yang manakah antara keadaan berikut menghasilkan nilai jangkaan terbesar $\\langle X \\rangle$?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "a. $|+\\rangle_x$\n"
msgstr "a. $|+\\rangle_x$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "b. $|-\\rangle_x$\n"
msgstr "b. $|-\\rangle_x$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "c. $|+\\rangle_y$ also called $|+i\\rangle$\n"
msgstr "c. $|+\\rangle_y$ juga dikenali sebagai $|+i\\rangle$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "d. $|-\\rangle_y$ also called $|-i\\rangle$\n"
msgstr "d. $|-\\rangle_y$ juga dikenali sebagai $|-i\\rangle$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "e. $|0\\rangle$ also called $|\\uparrow\\rangle$\n"
msgstr "e. $|0\\rangle$ juga dikenali sebagai $|\\uparrow\\rangle$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "f. $|1\\rangle$ also called $|\\downarrow\\rangle$\n"
msgstr "f. $|1\\rangle$ juga dikenali sebagai $|\\downarrow\\rangle$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Which of the following states yields the largest uncertainty $\\Delta X$?\n"
msgstr "Yang manakah antara keadaan berikut menghasilkan ketidakpastian terbesar $\\Delta X$?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "b. $|+\\rangle_y$ also called $|+i\\rangle$\n"
msgstr "b. $|+\\rangle_y$ juga dikenali sebagai $|+i\\rangle$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "c. $|0\\rangle$ also called $|\\uparrow\\rangle$\n"
msgstr "c. $|0\\rangle$ juga dikenali sebagai $|\\uparrow\\rangle$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "d. a and b are tied\n"
msgstr "d. a dan b seri\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "e. b and c are tied\n"
msgstr "e. b dan c seri\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "f. a, b, and c are tied\n"
msgstr "f. a, b, dan c seri\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Discussion Questions: {#discussion-questions}"
msgstr "Soalan Perbincangan: {#discussion-questions}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Does this concept of uncertainty conflict in any way with the notion of spin as a vector arrow in Cartesian space? How about on the Bloch sphere?\n"
msgstr "Adakah konsep ketidakpastian ini bercanggah dengan tanggapan spin sebagai anak panah vektor dalam ruang Cartesian? Bagaimana pula pada sfera Bloch?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose you orient a measurement device along a direction half-way between the $x$ and $y$ axes. What happens? Can you make a measurement along this direction? How does this relate to uncertainty in $X$ and $Y$?\n"
msgstr "Andaikan anda mengarahkan alat pengukuran ke arah yang berada di pertengahan antara paksi $x$ dan $y$. Apa yang berlaku? Bolehkah anda membuat pengukuran ke arah ini? Bagaimana ini berkaitan dengan ketidakpastian dalam $X$ dan $Y$?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "What additional experiments would you like to do to convince yourself of the results obtained here?\n"
msgstr "Apakah eksperimen tambahan yang ingin anda lakukan untuk meyakinkan diri anda tentang keputusan yang diperolehi di sini?\n"
